                <pb facs="0387" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/24355: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Algiers (Cole)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-23T22:00:00-04:00">September 23,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>287. From Murphy. Your 616, September 19, 11 a.m. Please advise Saint that this
                    information is useful and that we would like any additional data he may obtain
                    regarding Noguès’ present visit to Vichy.</p>
                <p>Any effort which can be made tactfully to ridicule the rumors of an American
                    landing would be appreciated. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
